      "text": " Timeline of Biology"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:14.777",
      "start": "00:00:08.711",
      "text": " How much do you know about the history and evolution of biology as a scientific discipline?"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:19.746",
      "start": "00:00:14.777",
      "text": " Let's take a look at a timeline of some important moments in biology."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:22.133",
      "start": "00:00:19.746",
      "text": " 347 BC"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:26.263",
      "start": "00:00:22.133",
      "text": " Aristotle began to classify living things into different groups"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:30.070",
      "start": "00:00:26.263",
      "text": " and is recognized today as the father of taxonomy."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:31.877",
      "start": "00:00:30.070",
      "text": " 1859"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:36.910",
      "start": "00:00:31.877",
      "text": " Charles Darwin published his theory of evolution, which states that humans evolved over a period"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:39.879",
      "start": "00:00:36.910",
      "text": " of time from simpler life forms."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:41.750",
      "start": "00:00:39.879",
      "text": " 1862"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:45.751",
      "start": "00:00:41.750",
      "text": " Louis Pasteur invented the process of pasteurization."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:51.558",
      "start": "00:00:45.751",
      "text": " This process kills bacteria and helps us to give beverages a longer shelf life."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:53.559",
      "start": "00:00:51.558",
      "text": " 1865"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:58.011",
      "start": "00:00:53.559",
      "text": " Gregor Mendel published his work on Mendelian inheritance."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:03.754",
      "start": "00:00:58.011",
      "text": " He performed experiments on pea plants that show how genes are inherited and expressed."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:05.755",
      "start": "00:01:03.754",
      "text": " 1900"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:09.497",
      "start": "00:01:05.755",
      "text": " Carl Lange-Diner discovered blood types."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:14.982",
      "start": "00:01:09.497",
      "text": " This helps us make sure that a person who needs a blood transfusion receives compatible blood."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:16.660",
      "start": "00:01:14.982",
      "text": " 1951"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:22.790",
      "start": "00:01:16.660",
      "text": " Rosalind Franklin captured photographs of DNA using x-ray crystallography, giving us clues"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:25.759",
      "start": "00:01:22.790",
      "text": " about its double helic structure."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:27.759",
      "start": "00:01:25.759",
      "text": " 1953"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:33.437",
      "start": "00:01:27.759",
      "text": " James Watson and Francis Crick published their findings on the structure of DNA using the"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:37.632",
      "start": "00:01:33.437",
      "text": " work of Rosalind Franklin and Maurice Wilkins."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:39.632",
      "start": "00:01:37.632",
      "text": " 1977"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:45.504",
      "start": "00:01:39.632",
      "text": " A microbiologist called Carl Wows discovered a new domain of life called R.K.R."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:47.505",
      "start": "00:01:45.504",
      "text": " 1978"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:50.860",
      "start": "00:01:47.505",
      "text": " The world's first test tube baby was born."
    },
    {
